Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Proves the Dirichlet identity with a function of the group sums: one
aggregate (shear s = Σw + x, Fubini, V2b's weighted simplex moment per
slice), two aggregates over the triangle, and the Fin N form with rough
set R and complement. Adds boundary cases (empty groups, zero exponents,
R < 0), rational polynomial specializations via V1's Lemma 10.1,
consistency with (10.1), the aggregate form of Lemma 9.2's endpoint on
V2b's translated pieces, a branch-type cut, and a worked example
(19/7680). Adds Comparator/aggregate_v2e.json, controls, the result
record and the V2e roadmap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DyEq5SJg3P8RhuwC4Kgon8
